WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.640
- Being a CEO or entrepreneur

00:00:01.640 --> 00:00:03.215
isn't something that you typically say

00:00:03.215 --> 00:00:04.325
that you wanna be when you grow up

00:00:04.325 --> 00:00:05.172
when you're younger.

00:00:05.172 --> 00:00:08.205
People wanna be basketball
players or like models

00:00:08.205 --> 00:00:10.409
'cause it's not very
glamorous to be a CEO.

00:00:10.409 --> 00:00:12.346
But we're proving that like it can be fun

00:00:12.346 --> 00:00:14.483
and like you can just
be like a normal person.

00:00:14.483 --> 00:00:19.283
(quirky music)

00:00:21.286 --> 00:00:22.331
I'm Erin.

00:00:22.331 --> 00:00:23.213
- And I'm Amelia.

00:00:23.213 --> 00:00:25.163
- And we run Shop Jeen together.

00:00:25.163 --> 00:00:27.439
- And we're best friends!
- And we're best friends.

00:00:27.439 --> 00:00:31.107
- So I started Shop Jeen in
my college dorm room 2012.

00:00:31.107 --> 00:00:32.454
And I was workin' retail jobs

00:00:32.454 --> 00:00:33.858
and just like kind of frustrated

00:00:33.858 --> 00:00:35.978
there wasn't like anything very cool

00:00:35.978 --> 00:00:39.355
for my taste online and to shop at.

00:00:39.355 --> 00:00:41.515
So Shop Jeen was born.

00:00:41.515 --> 00:00:43.790
We were really early to using Instagram

00:00:43.790 --> 00:00:46.832
and I like contribute a lot
of our success to Instagram.

00:00:46.832 --> 00:00:48.759
Started using it in 2012

00:00:48.759 --> 00:00:51.313
when not that many brands
or people were even on it.

00:00:51.313 --> 00:00:52.845
If you scroll pass one of our products

00:00:52.845 --> 00:00:54.331
you'll see it on the Explore page.

00:00:54.331 --> 00:00:56.352
It's like so eye-popping and catchy

00:00:56.352 --> 00:00:58.302
that like people definitely
like engage with it.

00:00:58.302 --> 00:01:01.204
- And we're really active on
our own personal social media

00:01:01.204 --> 00:01:03.596
like Instagram we use a lot.

00:01:03.596 --> 00:01:04.780
And yeah we just put like

00:01:04.780 --> 00:01:06.289
our kind of our whole lives out there.

00:01:06.289 --> 00:01:07.729
And I think our customers and fans

00:01:07.729 --> 00:01:09.424
like to relate to us on there.

00:01:09.424 --> 00:01:11.421
- Then 2012 I started Shop Jeen

00:01:11.421 --> 00:01:14.500
and then Amelia came on January 2013.

00:01:14.500 --> 00:01:16.543
- [Amelia] Yeah, so me
and Erin met years ago.

00:01:16.543 --> 00:01:18.958
We crossed paths interning
at Alexander Wang

00:01:18.958 --> 00:01:21.698
when we liked real fashion, right?

00:01:21.698 --> 00:01:22.929
- We read each other's vine,

00:01:22.929 --> 00:01:24.066
finish each other's sentences.

00:01:24.066 --> 00:01:25.506
We sleep in this bed together.

00:01:25.506 --> 00:01:26.179
- [Amelia] Oh yeah.

00:01:26.179 --> 00:01:28.269
- It's awesome to be
like business partners,

00:01:28.269 --> 00:01:32.448
sisters, best friends, low-key lovers.

00:01:32.448 --> 00:01:34.050
- It's almost three years now

00:01:34.050 --> 00:01:35.699
and we're not sick of each other yet,

00:01:35.699 --> 00:01:37.185
which is pretty crazy.

00:01:37.185 --> 00:01:40.737
The first thing that we
produced in-house ourselves

00:01:40.737 --> 00:01:42.432
was a line called NETGEAR90

00:01:42.432 --> 00:01:44.876
and it's an Internet-inspired

00:01:44.876 --> 00:01:47.842
really cool clothing and accessories line.

00:01:47.842 --> 00:01:50.234
The aesthetic of NETGEAR90 is just like

00:01:50.234 --> 00:01:51.372
Internet everything.

00:01:51.372 --> 00:01:53.299
It's inspired by Tumblr.

00:01:53.299 --> 00:01:56.951
There's lots of like baseball
caps with like reblog symbols

00:01:56.951 --> 00:01:59.797
and you know shirts that say Yes, Daddy?

00:01:59.797 --> 00:02:02.050
and things like that.

00:02:02.050 --> 00:02:04.116
- If I had to describe my personal style,

00:02:04.116 --> 00:02:08.110
it would be hardcore, poser.

00:02:08.110 --> 00:02:09.642
I love this shirt.

00:02:09.642 --> 00:02:11.693
"I'm retired. Do it yourself."

00:02:11.693 --> 00:02:13.505
Obnoxious, annoying.

00:02:13.505 --> 00:02:17.893
- I'm wearing a really cool,
double XL dinosaur hoodie.

00:02:17.893 --> 00:02:20.447
Ignorant and edgy.

00:02:20.447 --> 00:02:23.907
- Mine would be like thirsty
for attention probably.

00:02:23.907 --> 00:02:25.532
- These things are pretty cool.

00:02:25.532 --> 00:02:27.622
- We should take 'em on the plane.

00:02:27.622 --> 00:02:28.458
- Yeah.

00:02:28.458 --> 00:02:29.758
We would look like such idiots.

00:02:29.758 --> 00:02:30.756
Everyone will love it.

00:02:30.756 --> 00:02:31.546
- Perfect.

00:02:31.546 --> 00:02:34.657
- Our style changes like so constantly

00:02:34.657 --> 00:02:36.886
because we like know about things

00:02:36.886 --> 00:02:37.908
before they're big.

00:02:37.908 --> 00:02:40.114
We like also discard
them like very quickly

00:02:40.114 --> 00:02:42.343
because we're like, ew, we
just saw it like on this person

00:02:42.343 --> 00:02:43.364
or like everywhere.

00:02:43.364 --> 00:02:44.455
It's not cool anymore.

00:02:44.455 --> 00:02:46.034
- Yeah and it's fun, it's fun.

00:02:46.034 --> 00:02:47.010
We like dressing fun.

00:02:47.010 --> 00:02:49.823
People I feel like know that
we have a sense of humor

00:02:49.823 --> 00:02:52.214
and understand like pop culture

00:02:52.214 --> 00:02:53.491
and the Internet and stuff.

00:02:53.491 --> 00:02:55.186
- We definitely get people all the time

00:02:55.186 --> 00:02:56.440
who don't take us seriously

00:02:56.440 --> 00:02:57.462
because I mean look at us.

00:02:57.462 --> 00:02:58.878
We're in a bed full of pillows.

00:02:58.878 --> 00:03:01.144
The fact that we are very nonchalant

00:03:01.144 --> 00:03:02.212
and true to ourselves,

00:03:02.212 --> 00:03:04.464
we don't change for anyone.

00:03:04.464 --> 00:03:06.461
Like I will wear this to any meeting

00:03:06.461 --> 00:03:08.087
with any investor or anyone.

00:03:08.087 --> 00:03:09.898
There's no one I wouldn't
wear this outfit to.

00:03:09.898 --> 00:03:11.105
If that offends you

00:03:11.105 --> 00:03:12.963
then I don't think that
we should work together.

00:03:12.963 --> 00:03:14.658
The best part about running this business

00:03:14.658 --> 00:03:16.863
is the connection that we
have with our customers.

00:03:16.863 --> 00:03:18.416
We get comments in Instagram

00:03:18.416 --> 00:03:19.810
all the time.

00:03:19.810 --> 00:03:22.294
People saying that we have
like changed their lives

00:03:22.294 --> 00:03:24.151
that they don't feel like they belong

00:03:24.151 --> 00:03:25.846
and that when they come to our website,

00:03:25.846 --> 00:03:28.006
they feel like someone understands them.

00:03:28.006 --> 00:03:31.094
And to think about what
we're doing in that way

00:03:31.094 --> 00:03:33.068
that it's like inspiring people

00:03:33.068 --> 00:03:35.147
and like really impacting people's lives

00:03:35.147 --> 00:03:37.260
and making them more
comfortable with who they are

00:03:37.260 --> 00:03:39.791
able to express themselves through style

00:03:39.791 --> 00:03:42.486
and like fit in and like feel like

00:03:42.486 --> 00:03:44.058
it's okay to be just who they are

00:03:44.058 --> 00:03:45.614
like that is the most rewarding thing

00:03:45.614 --> 00:03:47.216
at the end of the day, hands down.

00:03:47.216 --> 00:03:51.355
- There's a rumor that we're
lesbians on the Internet.

00:03:51.355 --> 00:03:53.248
(laughs) Stop!

00:03:53.248 --> 00:03:54.200
So dramatic.

00:03:54.200 --> 00:03:55.265
- (laughs) I try.

